---
const { contactEmail } = Astro.props;
const cityJobsUrl = 'https://cityjobs.nyc.gov/jobs';
---

<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use govern your access to and use of the NYC Government Job Tracker mobile
      application, also displayed in parts of the App as NYC Jobs (the "App" or "Service"),
      provided by Restart Apps. By downloading, accessing, or using the App, you agree to these
      Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Purpose and Independent Status</h2>
    <p>
      The App helps users browse New York City government job listings, save jobs and searches,
      create local alerts and reminders, review hiring insights, and access official application
      pages. Posting data is retrieved from NYC Open Data.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App is independent and is not an official City of New York application. It is not
      affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or operated by the City of New York or any City
      agency.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the App only for lawful purposes and in compliance with applicable laws and
      platform rules. You agree not to misuse or disrupt the App, attempt unauthorized access,
      introduce harmful code, or reverse engineer it except where applicable law permits.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Job Information and Applications</h2>
    <p>
      Listings, salaries, requirements, deadlines, agency information, locations, hiring insights,
      and other employment information are provided for convenience and informational purposes.
      We do not guarantee that any information is complete, current, accurate, or still available.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for verifying every listing, deadline, qualification, and application
      requirement through <a href={cityJobsUrl}>official CityJobs</a> before relying on it or
      applying. Restart Apps is not an employer, recruiter, or party to any application or hiring
      decision and does not guarantee interviews or employment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Alerts, Reminders, and Saved Content</h2>
    <p>
      Alerts, notifications, reminders, saved jobs, and synced content are convenience features.
      We do not guarantee timely or successful delivery, inclusion of every matching opening, or
      permanent availability of saved or synced content. Monitor official sources for deadlines
      and changes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Optional account features use Google Sign-In or Sign in with Apple with Firebase
      Authentication. You are responsible for the security of your device and sign-in account. You
      may delete your App account from Settings or follow the
      <a href="/apps/nyc-government-jobs/delete-account">account-deletion instructions</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>NYCJobs Pro and In-App Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      The App may offer NYCJobs Pro as a one-time, non-subscription in-app purchase. The features,
      limits, and price shown on the purchase screen apply at the time of purchase. Purchases and
      restorations are processed by Google Play or Apple's App Store and remain subject to the
      applicable store account, payment, refund, and platform terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Restart Apps does not directly process payment-card information or control app-store refund
      decisions. You are responsible for using the correct store account. Deleting your App account
      does not automatically refund or erase a purchase maintained by an app store.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Third-Party Services and Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The App relies on third-party services including NYC Open Data, official CityJobs pages,
      Google and Apple sign-in services, Firebase, maps and location services, Google Play Billing,
      Apple StoreKit, Google AdMob, and consent tools. Third-party services, websites, ads, and
      stores are governed by their own terms and policies, and we are not responsible for their
      content, availability, security, or practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      The App's design, code, branding, and original materials are owned by Restart Apps or used
      with permission and are protected by applicable law. Government data, agency names,
      trademarks, and third-party materials remain the property of their respective owners.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Disclaimers and Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      The App is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, availability, merchantability, fitness
      for a particular purpose, non-infringement, or uninterrupted operation.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Restart Apps is not liable for indirect, incidental,
      special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost data, profits,
      opportunities, applications, interviews, or employment prospects arising from use of the
      App. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Changes and Contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these Terms and will update the effective date when changes take effect. Your
      continued use of the App after that date means you accept the revised Terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions may be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
